# Commercial S12.1 r2 pre-sync nginx baseline diagnosis

The complete read-only r2 server preflight reached nginx baseline validation
after the timer clock-domain correction. The installed site matched the
reviewed S10.1 final configuration SHA-256, but the preflight attempted to read
that reviewed file from the canonical Control checkout before the controller's
designed repository sync. The older detached checkout did not yet contain the
file, so the preflight stopped with no deployment attempt and no server
mutation.

The r3 correction compares the installed nginx site to a reviewed constant
instead of the unsynchronized checkout. Source validation proves the constant
matches the reviewed baseline bytes, and freeze provenance independently binds
the baseline artifact. The immutable r1 and r2 tags remain unchanged.
